<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hadoti</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Harauti</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hadoti is a region of south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajasthan">Rajasthan</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, around the cities of Kota, Bundi, Baran and Jhalawar. It takes its name from the Hada <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chauhan">Chauhan Rajputs</a>, who ruled the states of Bundi and Kota there from the 14th century. The region lies on a plateau drained by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chambal-river">Chambal River</a> and has its own dialect, Harauti.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hadoti.jpg" alt="Hadoti" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Alvin Antony 910 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Garh_Palace,_Bundi,_Rajasthan.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
